<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?><!--
  Definition of the routines widget: one tile per enabled routine tracker
  (workout, medication and supplement), one per row, each one marking the day
  done or not done in place - the same toggle of the home cards, straight from
  the launcher.

  How the size works: a launcher places widgets on a grid of cells, so the size
  is expressed in cells and the launcher translates it to dp.
  - targetCellWidth/targetCellHeight are the size used by launchers on
    Android 12+ (2 columns by 3 rows here: the two columns of the 2x2 grid of
    tiles - two routines side by side, two rows at most - plus room around it).
  - minWidth/minHeight are the same size in dp, using the formula launchers rely
    on (70dp * cells - 30dp): minWidth = 70*2 - 30 = 110dp,
    minHeight = 70*3 - 30 = 180dp.
  - minResizeWidth/minResizeHeight are the floor of a resize: 2 columns by 2
    rows, the smallest size where the name still fits beside the icon box;
    below that the text would be cut again.
  - resizeMode allows resizing in both directions. The card of tiles hugs its
    grid and centers in the cell (a hidden routine collapses with its cell, see
    the layout), so a bigger cell just adds room around it.
  - updatePeriodMillis keeps the tiles on the day shown: the launcher asks for an
    update at most every 30 minutes (the smallest interval allowed), which is
    also what rolls the widget over to the new day after midnight.
  - previewLayout makes the picker show the real widget instead of an image.
-->
<appwidget-provider xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:description="@string/widget_tracker_description"
    android:initialLayout="@layout/widget_tracker"
    android:minWidth="120dp"
    android:minHeight="70dp"
    android:previewLayout="@layout/widget_tracker"
    android:resizeMode="horizontal|vertical"
    android:targetCellWidth="3"
    android:targetCellHeight="1"
    android:updatePeriodMillis="1800000"
    android:widgetCategory="home_screen" />
